# Compile input for requirements.lock — the hash-locked portion of the
# ytmusic-streamer image.
#
# This is every dependency the image needs EXCEPT the two deliberately-exempt
# packages, yt-dlp and ytmusicapi (see requirements-exempt.txt for why). Those
# two are installed loose, AFTER this lock, so a YouTube breakage can be fixed
# with a same-day floor bump without regenerating the lock.
#
# `requests` is ytmusicapi's only runtime dependency, and brotli,
# pycryptodomex, and websockets are the stable dependencies of yt-dlp's
# `default` extra (certifi/mutagen/requests/urllib3 are already here via other
# routes). They are pinned+hashed so that when the exempt install runs, ONLY
# yt-dlp, ytmusicapi, and yt-dlp-ejs themselves are unpinned — the rest of
# their transitive tree is already fixed by this lock. yt-dlp-ejs cannot be
# locked because each yt-dlp release pins it exactly (==), so it must float
# with yt-dlp.
#
# Regenerate the lock: see the header of requirements.lock.
fastapi>=0.141.1
uvicorn>=0.52.3
mutagen>=1.48.1
pydantic>=2.13.4
httpx>=0.28.1
requests>=2.34.2
# yt-dlp[default] stable extras (see requirements-exempt.txt)
brotli>=1.2.0
